\fs36 \cf0 Three scripts assist with importing/managing Apple Lossless audio files and sending converted AAC copies to iPod.\
\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Lossless to AAC Workflow (CD->iPod)
\f0\b0 :\
\'a5 Imports each enabled CD track as an Apple Lossless file\
\'a5 Makes a converted AAC 
\f1\b copy
\f0\b0  of each imported Lossless file\
\'a5 Adds the AAC file to iPod, 
\f1\b deleting
\f0\b0  the original AAC from iTunes.\
\

\f1\b Lossless to AAC Workflow (iTunes->iPod)
\f0\b0 :\
\'a5 Makes a converted AAC 
\f1\b copy
\f0\b0  of each Lossless track selected in iTunes\
\'a5 Adds the AAC file to iPod, 
\f1\b deleting
\f0\b0  the original AAC from iTunes.\
\

\f1\b Sync Tags of iPod AACs with iTunes Lossless
\f0\b0 :\
\'a5 Attempts to sync your choice of Rating, Play Count, and/or Played Date data between corresponding iPod AAC tracks and Apple Lossless tracks in iTunes.\
\
In this way you can keep archived Lossless files on your hard drive, and manageable AAC files on your iPod.\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li200\fi-20\ql\qnatural

