\f1\b\fs24 \cf2 How to use:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
Put each script in your iTunes Scripts folder. This is located in 
\f2\i \cf3 user name
\f0\i0  > Library > iTunes\cf0 . If there is no folder named "Scripts" there, create one and put the scripts in it. They will then appear in iTunes' Script menu, where you can activate each by clicking on its name.\
\
\
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural

\f1\b \cf0 Lossless to AAC Workflow (CD->iPod):
\f0\b0 \
\
Insert a CD, select it in iTunes, and check-mark the CD tracks you want to import. Run the script and this list of preferences will be displayed:\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\ql\qnatural
\cf0 {{\NeXTGraphic Pasted Graphic 1.tiff \width5480 \height4280
}¬}\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\ql\qnatural
\cf0 \
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural
\cf0 Select each of the actions you want to perform:\
\

\f1\b \'a5 Import as Apple Lossless
\f0\b0  - import each check-marked CD track as an Apple Lossless audio file.\
\

\f1\b \'a5 Convert to AAC
\f0\b0  - make an AAC copy of each Apple Lossless file.\
\

\f1\b \'a5 Add AACs to iPod
\f0\b0  - 
\f2\i displayed if an iPod is mounted
\f0\i0  - Add each AAC file to the iPod and delete the original AAC track in iTunes and delete its file from your hard drive.\
\

\f1\b \'a5 Create New iPod Playlist
\f0\b0  - 
\f2\i displayed if an iPod is mounted
\f0\i0  - Make a new iPod playlist and copy the AAC tracks to it. You will be asked to provide a name for the new iPod playlist. The default iPod playlist name will be "
\f2\i Artist - Album
\f0\i0 ", obtained from the CD.\
\

\f1\b \'a5 Eject CD
\f0\b0  - When finished, eject the CD.\
\
For your convenience, your chosen preferences will be remembered the next time you run the script.\
\
\

