\f1\b \cf0 Sync Tags of iPod AACs with iTunes Lossless
\f0\b0 \
\
This applet will allow you to copy your choice of Rating, Play Count, and Played Date between the AACs on your iPod and the corresponding Lossless tracks in iTunes, or visa versa.\
\
This script identifies corresponding tracks by using each track's Song Name, Artist, Album, and Time. As such, it is 
\f2\i possible
\f0\i0  for the script to fail if these data do not match.\
\
Select some AAC tracks on the iPod or Lossless tracks in iTunes. These are the tracks whose data will be copied. If you have 
\f1\b no tracks
\f0\b0  specifically selected, the script will assume you want to use the entire library chosen in the second dialog box below. This can take a long time depending on how many tracks are in your library, so I recommend using a selection.\
\
Next, choose which tags you want copied:\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\ql\qnatural\pardirnatural
\cf0 {{\NeXTGraphic 1__#$!@%!#__Pasted Graphic.tiff \width4520 \height4000
}¬}\cf0 \
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural
\
Then, choose which direction to sync the tag data to (make sure you choose the correct direction!):\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\ql\qnatural\pardirnatural
\cf0 {{\NeXTGraphic Pasted Graphic 2.tiff \width11640 \height2720
}¬}\cf0 \
\pard\tx160\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\li180\ql\qnatural
\
The script will try to locate the corresponding tracks and copy your selected data.\
\
\cf0 \
