\f1\b \cf2 Notes:
\f0\b0 \cf0 \
\
\'a5 I cannot eliminate the "done-chime" that sounds after each import and convert. Try using the script {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dougscripts.com/itunes/scripts/ss.php?sp=ihatethatitunesdonechime"}}{\fldrslt I Hate That iTunes Done Chime!}} which will let you set a System sound, no sound, or your own AIFF sound for the "done-chime.\
\
\'a5 Each import/convert script takes care of changing encoders and will restore your Preferences-set encoder when finished.\
\
\'a5 Your "Importing" preferences will be in force and your 
\f1\b current
\f0\b0  AAC encoder settings will be used to convert the Lossless file. You might want to double-check these in the "Importing" pane of iTunes Preferences.\
\
\'a5 The capacity of the iPod is checked before copying each AAC file to it. If you don't have enough space, you will be alerted.\
\
\'a5 To cancel a script, click on the the "x" next to the progress bar in iTunes' display area.\
\
